# A database a test fixture left behind. Fixtures write theirs under
# Path.GetTempPath()/chalk-tests/ now (D133 §0c) and assert that before they open
# one, so nothing here should ever match -- this is the net under the assertion,
# widened after ":memory:chalk-<guid>" turned out to be a *file name* to
# DuckDB.NET and slipped past the previous pattern. Twice, at the repository root
# and under dotnet/, because a test process's working directory is its own bin/
# and a tool's is wherever it was started.
chalk-*.db*
:memory:*
*.duckdb
/dotnet/:memory:*
/dotnet/*.duckdb
/dotnet/chalk-*.db*

# ...and the one thing that pattern must not catch. On a case-insensitive file
# system `*.duckdb` matches the directory `Chalk.Sources.DuckDb`, which is a
# package and not a stray database.
!/dotnet/src/Chalk.Sources.DuckDb/

# Worktrees that parallel agents create under the repository; never content of the project
.claude/worktrees/

# NuGet packages written by scripts/pack.sh
dist/
